-Figure~\ref{fig:architecture} illustrates MynaNet~v1. The network comprises:
+Figure~\ref{fig:architecture} illustrates MynaNet (model~1j). The network
+comprises:
 \begin{enumerate}
-  \item \textbf{Stem:} Conv2D(128, $3\times3$) + BatchNorm + ReLU6.
-  \item \textbf{Four DS-Conv-SE blocks} with residual connections and
-        $2\times2$ max-pooling, channel widths [120, 180, 146, 360].
-        Blocks 2--4 use $1\times1$ projection in the skip path when channel
-        counts change.
-  \item \textbf{Lightweight MHSA:} Projects 360-dim features to 88-dim;
-        2 heads with $d_k=32$; attention over $5\times18=90$ patches.
-        LayerNorm applied after residual add.
-  \item \textbf{Head:} GlobalAveragePooling $\to$ Dense(176) + BatchNorm +
-        ReLU6 + Dropout(0.05) $\to$ Dense(10) + Softmax.
+  \item \textbf{Stem:} Conv2D(32, $3\times3$) + BatchNorm + ReLU6.
+  \item \textbf{Four MBV3-style inverted-residual SE blocks,} each followed
+        by MaxPool2D($2\times2$) and Dropout.  Output channels: 16, 24, 48,
+        96.  Blocks~1--2 use $3\times3$ depthwise convolutions; Blocks~3--4
+        use $5\times5$ depthwise convolutions for a wider spectro-temporal
+        receptive field.  Expand ratios: $t=1$ (Block~1), $t=6$
+        (Blocks~2--4).
+  \item \textbf{Last-stage expansion:} Conv2D(320, $1\times1$) + BatchNorm
+        + ReLU6 before global pooling.
+  \item \textbf{Head:} GlobalAveragePooling $\to$ Dense(128) + BatchNorm +
+        ReLU6 + Dropout $\to$ Dense(12) + Softmax.
 \end{enumerate}
 
